// @run
// @log 7
// D-PARSETY P1: the module merge rewrites the parser's SPELLING TREE and renders
// the annotation name from it, instead of scanning the rendered string for
// identifier runs. The tree knows a `TS_FIELD`'s text is a FIELD name (and a
// `TS_LITSTR`'s a literal lexeme), so only genuine type positions — `TS_NAME`,
// `TS_APP`'s head, a `TS_MAP`'s key — rename.
//
// On the string scanner this program failed with `cannot assign {v: i32} to 'h'
// of type {v: i32}` / `no field 'v' on {v: i32}` — two types that RENDER the same
// because the diagnostic demangler strips the `$m1` the field name had grown.
import { mk } from "./lib"

const h = mk()
print(h.v)
